{"chapter": "stacks-properties", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "04XB", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-properties-morphisms}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:5f139f95cb2944f2b4a50c57c9c441ebf931ffcef0e4702ba9f8ee0da4b5a3e2", "source_text": "Properties of morphisms representable by algebraic spaces", "source_text_hash": "sha256:324e340ee083edfcab458af08117ffc98655b826046069338156a5f829353b53", "unit_id": "tag:04XB:title"}
{"chapter": "stacks-properties", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "04XB", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$X \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "STRUCT_0002": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0003": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:0ab03208407fbc5a774c8a98da3350fe725ca1399eb21f4802ee9362c63d3b0f", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:471462c83271475c4526fe8883b3e2416c123882f2ac4a24d4dd19d7df28467e", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nWe will study properties of (arbitrary) morphisms of algebraic stacks in its\nown chapter. For morphisms representable by algebraic spaces we know what\nit means to be surjective, smooth, or <ACCENT_0001>tale, etc. This applies in particular\nto morphisms <MATH_0001> from algebraic spaces to algebraic stacks.\nIn this section, we recall how this works, we list the properties to which\nthis applies, and we prove a few easy lemmas.\n\n<STRUCT_0002><STRUCT_0003>\nOur first lemma says a morphism is representable by algebraic spaces\nif it is so after a base change by a flat,\nlocally finitely presented, surjective morphism.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:d18c8f8193e21a3197c67fbb507b1587ddba8e4977b446d4abb34cecbf768fb7", "unit_id": "tag:04XB:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "stacks-properties", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "04XB", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : \\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0002": "$W$", "MATH_0003": "$W \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0004": "$f$", "MATH_0005": "$W \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{X}$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-check-representable-covering}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:7932f955e76c5a3746308199a36c32ae2f02e91ea163f462fdca6c24f0c8e997", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:0c209326d6de8816248ccdcf05b69e43e1fb9bf2eaf9069c232ccf9c2997cbe7", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism of algebraic stacks.\nLet <MATH_0002> be an algebraic space and let <MATH_0003> be surjective,\nlocally of finite presentation, and flat. The following are equivalent\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> <MATH_0004> is representable by algebraic spaces, and\n<STRUCT_0003> <MATH_0005> is an algebraic space.\n<STRUCT_0004>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:cf5821849bd38168ec6a0daf1f6b61b41080c0ac39b81000ee347385e030e8d7", "unit_id": "tag:04ZP:statement"}
{"chapter": "stacks-properties", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "04XB", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\Rightarrow$", "MATH_0002": "$W \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0003": "$f$", "MATH_0004": "$W \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{X} \\to W$", "MATH_0005": "$f$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{algebraic-lemma-base-change-by-space-representable-by-space}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{algebraic-lemma-characterize-representable-by-algebraic-spaces}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{stacks-lemma-faithful-descent}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:e95c1419676e899d1bc55dd8ca367ab01afb492fdb7433bed9896ed5570a6857", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:07c4cde2ee9f6fb359e9503c164bed1df13743b5b81f5f971baf2db542aa90d6", "source_text": "The implication (1) <MATH_0001> (2) is\nAlgebraic Stacks,\nLemma <REF_0001>.\nConversely, let <MATH_0002> be as in (2). To prove (1) it\nsuffices to show that <MATH_0003> is faithful on fibre categories, see\nAlgebraic Stacks,\nLemma <REF_0002>.\nAssumption (2) implies in particular that\n<MATH_0004> is faithful.\nHence the faithfulness of <MATH_0005> follows from\nStacks, Lemma <REF_0003>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:1f86a0c347537ffb6fb626eca4f5388b21a0b44f68561db0b12b8895d1a705e1", "unit_id": "tag:04ZP:proof"}
